{%- comment -%}
  theinmag-bundle-tile
  Single product tile, rendered in two contexts. Pass a product (and
  optional context):

    {% render 'theinmag-bundle-tile', product: product %}                  (bundle, default)
    {% render 'theinmag-bundle-tile', product: product, context: 'shop' %}

  Bundle context (BaB picker):
    - Cover + title are NOT wrapped in a link.
    - Add buttons fire data-bundle-add (picker's updateBundleUI()).
    - aria-labels carry "...to bundle" suffix.

  Shop context (/shop product grid):
    - Cover + title wrap in <a> linking to PDP.
    - Second cover image (digital edition) renders from
      product.metafields.single_mag.digital_media_images first slot when
      present. Parent grid toggles data-active-format on its wrapper; CSS
      swaps which cover is visible. Pattern matches the single-mag PDP
      iPad-mockup swap (theinmag-single-mags-hero.liquid).
    - Pre-sale / Current-issue badge (peach / mint pill) renders in the
      title row, right-aligned beside the title, driven by
      product.metafields.theinmag.is_pre_order (pre-sale) or the
      shop.metafields.theinmag.current_issue_number match (current issue).
    - Add buttons fire data-shop-add (shop-grid's AJAX add-to-cart).
    - Aria-labels carry "...to cart" suffix.

  Variant lookup is unchanged: scan product.variants for option titles
  containing "Print" or "Digital" (case-insensitive). Defensive ordering
  Print-then-Digital matches the BaB picker's row order.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign tile_context = context | default: 'bundle'

  comment
    Optional shop-context override: a filename of an asset in /assets/ used
    as the PRINT cover instead of product.featured_image. Lets the shop grid
    show a curated cover for a product (e.g. Membership) without touching the
    product's featured image in admin. Ignored outside the shop context.

    digital_cover_filename does the same for the DIGITAL cover - used when a
    product has no single_mag.digital_media_images metafield (e.g. Membership)
    so the grid still has something to swap to under the Digital filter.
  endcomment
  assign cover_override = cover_filename | default: ''
  assign digital_cover_override = digital_cover_filename | default: ''

  assign print_variant = null
  assign digital_variant = null
  for v in product.variants
    assign vt = v.title | downcase
    if print_variant == null and vt contains 'print'
      assign print_variant = v
    elsif digital_variant == null and vt contains 'digital'
      assign digital_variant = v
    endif
  endfor

  assign cover_image = product.featured_image
  assign tile_title = product.title | replace: 'theINmag - ', '' | replace: 'theINmag ', ''

  assign digital_cover_image = null
  assign is_pre_order = false
  assign pdp_url = ''
  if tile_context == 'shop'
    assign digital_media_images = product.metafields.single_mag.digital_media_images.value
    if digital_media_images != blank
      for img in digital_media_images
        if forloop.first
          assign digital_cover_image = img
        endif
      endfor
    endif
    assign is_pre_order = product.metafields.theinmag.is_pre_order | default: false
    # Current-issue badge - driven by the theinmag.current_issue_number
    # shop metafield (stored like "Mag09"). Matched against the product
    # handle (lowercased). A pre-order issue is never the current issue,
    # so that case is excluded. Update the one metafield each drop and
    # the badge moves itself - no theme edit needed.
    assign is_current_issue = false
    assign current_issue_mf = shop.metafields.theinmag.current_issue_number.value
    if current_issue_mf != blank and is_pre_order == false
      assign current_issue_handle = current_issue_mf | downcase
      if product.handle == current_issue_handle
        assign is_current_issue = true
      endif
    endif
    # Pre-sale drop date - single source of truth is the shop metafield
    # theinmag.next_release_date (YYYY-MM-DD), the same one the cart badge
    # reads. Formats to "15 June". Update that one metafield each drop and
    # every pre-sale badge sitewide moves with it - no theme edit needed.
    # Blank metafield falls back to a bare "Pre-sale" (no date).
    assign presale_date = ''
    if is_pre_order
      assign next_release_date = shop.metafields.theinmag.next_release_date.value
      if next_release_date != blank
        assign presale_date = next_release_date | date: '%-d %B'
      endif
    endif
    assign pdp_url = '/products/' | append: product.handle
    assign add_suffix = ' to cart'
    assign add_attr = 'data-shop-add'
    # Peek mode (stockist picker): build a pipe-joined list of preview image
    # URLs - the print cover first, then this issue's inside_gallery_images
    # (same source the INside section uses). JS opens these in a lightbox so
    # the shopper never leaves the page. Blank list = no peek (link falls back).
    if peek
      assign peek_urls = ''
      assign peek_inside = product.metafields.single_mag.inside_gallery_images.value
      for img in peek_inside
        assign peek_one = img | image_url: width: 1200
        if peek_urls == blank
          assign peek_urls = peek_one
        else
          assign peek_urls = peek_urls | append: '|' | append: peek_one
        endif
      endfor
      # Fallback only: a product with NO inside gallery (e.g. Snack Pack)
      # still opens the lightbox showing its cover, so it never leaves the
      # page. Mags with a gallery lead with their own first image (the
      # styled cover), no plain-cover double-up of the tile.
      if peek_urls == blank
        if cover_override != blank
          assign peek_urls = cover_override | asset_url
        elsif cover_image != blank
          assign peek_urls = cover_image | image_url: width: 1200
        endif
      endif
    endif
    # Peek is offered ONLY for genuine issues, NEVER membership: the peek's
    # add-to-cart would post the membership variant with no _starting_mag
    # (the #51018 incident). Membership keeps its 'Join the club' picker CTA.
    assign peek_enabled = false
    if peek and peek_urls != blank and product.handle != 'membership'
      assign peek_enabled = true
    endif
  else
    assign add_suffix = ' to bundle'
    assign add_attr = 'data-bundle-add'
  endif
-%}

<article
  class="theinmag-bundle-tile{% if tile_context == 'shop' %} theinmag-bundle-tile--shop{% endif %}"
  data-bundle-tile
  data-product-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
  data-context="{{ tile_context }}"
  {%- if tile_context == 'shop' %} data-pre-order="{{ is_pre_order }}"{%- endif %}
>
  <div class="theinmag-bundle-tile__cover">
    {%- if tile_context == 'shop' -%}
      <a href="{{ pdp_url }}" class="theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-link{% if peek_enabled %} theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-link--peek{% endif %}" aria-label="{% if peek_enabled %}Peek inside {{ tile_title }}{% else %}View {{ tile_title }}{% endif %}"{% if peek_enabled %} data-peek-trigger data-peek-images="{{ peek_urls | escape }}" data-peek-title="{{ tile_title | escape }}" data-peek-url="{{ pdp_url }}" data-peek-variant="{{ print_variant.id }}"{% if print_variant %} data-peek-variant-print="{{ print_variant.id }}" data-peek-price-print="{{ print_variant.price | money | escape }}"{% if stockist_pricing %} data-peek-rrp-print="{{ print_variant.price }}"{% endif %}{% if print_variant.available == false %} data-peek-print-soldout="true"{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if digital_variant and print_only != true %} data-peek-variant-digital="{{ digital_variant.id }}" data-peek-price-digital="{{ digital_variant.price | money | escape }}"{% endif %}{% endif %}>
        {%- if cover_override != blank -%}
          <img
            class="theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-img theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-img--print"
            src="{{ cover_override | asset_url }}"
            alt="{{ product.title | escape }} print cover"
            width="480"
            height="640"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- elsif cover_image != blank -%}
          <img
            class="theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-img theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-img--print"
            src="{{ cover_image | image_url: width: 480 }}"
            srcset="{{ cover_image | image_url: width: 320 }} 320w, {{ cover_image | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ cover_image | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w"
            sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 25vw, (min-width: 750px) 33vw, 50vw"
            alt="{{ product.title | escape }} print cover"
            width="480"
            height="640"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if digital_cover_override != blank -%}
          <img
            class="theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-img theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-img--digital"
            src="{{ digital_cover_override | asset_url }}"
            alt="{{ product.title | escape }} digital edition"
            width="480"
            height="640"
            loading="lazy"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
        {%- elsif digital_cover_image != blank -%}
          <img
            class="theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-img theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-img--digital"
            src="{{ digital_cover_image | image_url: width: 480 }}"
            srcset="{{ digital_cover_image | image_url: width: 320 }} 320w, {{ digital_cover_image | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ digital_cover_image | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w"
            sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 25vw, (min-width: 750px) 33vw, 50vw"
            alt="{{ product.title | escape }} digital edition"
            width="480"
            height="640"
            loading="lazy"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if peek_enabled -%}
          <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__peek-hint" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 12s3.5-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-3.5 7-10 7-10-7-10-7z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg>
            Peek inside
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </a>
      {%- if is_pre_order -%}
        <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__ribbon theinmag-bundle-tile__ribbon--presale" aria-label="On pre-sale{% if presale_date != blank %}, drops {{ presale_date }}{% endif %}">
          <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__ribbon-top">Pre-sale</span>
          {%- if presale_date != blank -%}
            <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__ribbon-sub">Drops {{ presale_date }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      {%- elsif is_current_issue -%}
        <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__ribbon theinmag-bundle-tile__ribbon--current" aria-label="Current issue">Current issue</span>
      {%- elsif product.handle == 'digital-stack' -%}
        {%- liquid
          # Value ribbon (2026-08-11): the Digital Stack's savings against
          # buying each digital issue one at a time, computed live so the
          # price change and each new drop keep it honest.
          assign ds_anchor = 0
          assign ds_count = 0
          for ds_issue in collections['single-issues'].products
            assign ds_inum = ds_issue.metafields.single_mag.issue_number.value | default: 0
            assign ds_pre = ds_issue.metafields.theinmag.is_pre_order | default: false
            if ds_inum > 0 and ds_pre == false
              for ds_v in ds_issue.variants
                if ds_v.option1 == 'Digital'
                  assign ds_anchor = ds_anchor | plus: ds_v.price
                  assign ds_count = ds_count | plus: 1
                  break
                endif
              endfor
            endif
          endfor
          assign ds_save = ds_anchor | minus: product.price
        -%}
        {%- if ds_save > 0 -%}
          <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__ribbon theinmag-bundle-tile__ribbon--value" aria-label="All {{ ds_count }} issues, save {{ ds_save | money }}">
            <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__ribbon-top">Save {{ ds_save | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
            <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__ribbon-sub">All {{ ds_count }} issues</span>
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- if cover_image != blank -%}
        <img
          src="{{ cover_image | image_url: width: 480 }}"
          srcset="{{ cover_image | image_url: width: 320 }} 320w, {{ cover_image | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ cover_image | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w"
          sizes="(min-width: 990px) 240px, 160px"
          alt="{{ product.title | escape }} cover"
          width="480"
          height="640"
          loading="lazy"
        >
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="theinmag-bundle-tile__cover-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if tile_context == 'shop' -%}
    <div class="theinmag-bundle-tile__title-row">
      <a href="{{ pdp_url }}" class="theinmag-bundle-tile__title-link">
        <h3 class="theinmag-bundle-tile__title">{{ tile_title }}</h3>
      </a>
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <h3 class="theinmag-bundle-tile__title">{{ tile_title }}</h3>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Membership tile has 3 selector axes (Format / Length / Starting Issue)
    that don't fit a two-row add-to-cart pattern, so on /shop it gets a
    single CTA that opens the membership picker popup
    (snippets/theinmag-membership-popup.liquid). Routed for the membership
    product in EVERY context (not just shop) so it can never fall through to
    a generic Add button that would omit properties[_starting_mag] - the
    starting issue lives in the popup/form. The BaB picker never includes the
    membership product anyway.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if product.handle == 'membership' -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="theinmag-bundle-tile__join"
      data-membership-popup-trigger
      aria-haspopup="dialog"
      aria-label="Choose options and join the club"
    >Join the club</button>
  {%- else -%}

    {%- if print_variant -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign print_sold_out = false
        if print_variant.available == false
          assign print_sold_out = true
        endif
      -%}
      <div class="theinmag-bundle-tile__row theinmag-bundle-tile__row--print{% if print_sold_out %} is-sold-out{% endif %}{% if print_only %} theinmag-bundle-tile__row--qty{% endif %}" data-variant-id="{{ print_variant.id }}"{% if stockist_pricing %} data-rrp-price="{{ print_variant.price }}"{% endif %}>
        <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__format">Print</span>
        {%- if print_sold_out -%}
          <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__pill" aria-label="Print sold out">Sold out</span>
        {%- else -%}
          {%- if stockist_pricing -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Stockist picker: both prices on the tile. The stockist figure is
              filled in by theinmag-stockist-pricing.js ONLY once it has read
              the entered code's real value off the live cart, so an empty
              element here means we have no confirmed rate and retail is all
              we show.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__price theinmag-bundle-tile__price-stack">
              <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__stockist-price" data-stockist-price hidden></span>
              <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__price-rrp"><span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__rrp">RRP</span> {{ print_variant.price | money }}</span>
            </span>
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__price">{% if print_only %}<span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__rrp">RRP</span> {% endif %}{{ print_variant.price | money }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if print_only -%}
            <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__buy">
              <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__qty">
                <button type="button" class="theinmag-bundle-tile__qty-btn" data-tile-minus aria-label="Decrease quantity">&#8722;</button>
                <input type="text" class="theinmag-bundle-tile__qty-input" data-tile-qty value="1" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" aria-label="Quantity for {{ tile_title }}">
                <button type="button" class="theinmag-bundle-tile__qty-btn" data-tile-plus aria-label="Increase quantity">+</button>
              </span>
              <button type="button" class="theinmag-bundle-tile__add" {{ add_attr }} data-variant-id="{{ print_variant.id }}" aria-label="Add {{ tile_title }} Print{{ add_suffix }}"><span data-add-label>Add</span><span data-added-label hidden>Added &#10003;</span></button>
            </span>
          {%- else -%}
            <button type="button" class="theinmag-bundle-tile__add" {{ add_attr }} data-variant-id="{{ print_variant.id }}" aria-label="Add {{ tile_title }} Print{{ add_suffix }}"><span data-add-label>Add</span><span data-added-label hidden>Added &#10003;</span></button>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} print_only (stockist picker) suppresses the Digital buy row. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if digital_variant and print_only != true -%}
      <div class="theinmag-bundle-tile__row theinmag-bundle-tile__row--digital" data-variant-id="{{ digital_variant.id }}">
        <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__format">Digital</span>
        <span class="theinmag-bundle-tile__price">{{ digital_variant.price | money }}</span>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="theinmag-bundle-tile__add"
          {{ add_attr }}
          data-variant-id="{{ digital_variant.id }}"
          aria-label="Add {{ tile_title }} Digital{{ add_suffix }}"
        ><span data-add-label>Add</span><span data-added-label hidden>Added &#10003;</span></button>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Optional one-line blurb under the buy controls (Ryan, 2026-08-12:
    the Membership and Digital Stack tiles said nothing about what they
    ARE). Passed in by the shop grid from its own settings; blank on
    every other product and in non-shop contexts.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if blurb != blank and tile_context == 'shop' -%}
    <p class="theinmag-bundle-tile__blurb">{{ blurb }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
</article>
